Package: glmap
Title: High-Performance GPU Geospatial Mapping for 'sf' and 'terra'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Beneva", "Geospatial Team", , "geospatial@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Mapbox", role = "cph", comment = "mapbox/earcut.hpp in src/earcut.h"))
Description: A compact, high-performance WebGL2 and 'MapLibre GL' interactive
    mapping engine for R designed as a next-generation GPU alternative to 'leaflet'.
    Bypasses 'htmlwidgets' JSON bottlenecks by streaming zero-copy 'GLMP' and
    'GeoArrow' binary vertex/attribute buffers directly from C++17 to WebGL2 GPU
    shaders, with C++ 'mapbox/earcut' polygon hole triangulation, in-memory spatial
    R-tree dynamic viewport slicing, 'DuckDB' out-of-core Parquet pushdown, live
    GPU fragment shaders for 'terra' rasters (0ms colormaps, hillshading,
    contrast stretching, and band math), full 'Shiny' proxy diffing, 'crosstalk'
    linked brushing, and a modular plugin architecture.
URL: https://meztez.github.io/glmap/, https://github.com/meztez/glmap
BugReports: https://github.com/meztez/glmap/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
